{"event_type":"review","id":"3626696b4c8d5e1744b686d92f776e5296b301aa0efa5b9eb0981a2ae8845d00","occurred_at":"2026-11-11T23:40:29Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cfa29ac18cbbc48917096aeaa4f364be04271e5414b48472f10b76c50e456c2b","sha256":"cfa29ac18cbbc48917096aeaa4f364be04271e5414b48472f10b76c50e456c2b"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1567bf15a099407a5f851e18e726cd5ffe02a14103666b0910f9fa53e06a208a","sha256":"1567bf15a099407a5f851e18e726cd5ffe02a14103666b0910f9fa53e06a208a"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1d370a6a418758f793db784dd889aa33a42dcfce6aaa86389f207bea869656da","sha256":"1d370a6a418758f793db784dd889aa33a42dcfce6aaa86389f207bea869656da"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/26ad58bc6b7935efbfd7a6d93f4cc4025631710f9db7d9e11d2e975217e8fef6","sha256":"26ad58bc6b7935efbfd7a6d93f4cc4025631710f9db7d9e11d2e975217e8fef6"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/78b9760bbf0480fa9a15c3f76afa75f52ed0cea25dc767b9688bc0a5b0586ca6","sha256":"78b9760bbf0480fa9a15c3f76afa75f52ed0cea25dc767b9688bc0a5b0586ca6"}],"attempt_id":"69131df53fdabd49d5055ee899884a6ec22a0685c00ce84a28c06efb34bc3a99:0:1","base":"50f62ddc48f9347a9fd96fb645e43982a9f3e75d","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"6bab0c2a318551d8629b312c4d7207e80efe1cbb","body":"**Freeze the validated source before the startup waits.**\n\nIn `apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch.py`, Line 2821 validates commit A before image preparation and guest startup. If another process switches the checkout to commit B during those waits, this command archives B, but the report still declares A. Uploads also read the live checkout.\n\nIf the guest proof script is unchanged between A and B, verification can accept this mixed-source run. The verifier does not bind the archive to the declared commit.\n\nCapture an immutable source snapshot before the waits. Upload from that snapshot and pass the validated SHA to `git archive`.","id":"4d8be923d8968d97b0f8960425374dd1591ec4b4607a177ddbddf38e84642c42","intervals":[[285,285]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch.py","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Freeze the validated source before the startup waits."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"6bab0c2a318551d8629b312c4d7207e80efe1cbb","body":"**Compare the fence-phase state digests with the prepared baseline.**\n\nThe `inspect` snapshot is already compared with `prepared.state` in `build_checks`. The final `fence` phase runs after `inspect`. Its guest payload retains its own `queue.json` and `heartbeat.json` digests, but no base or matrix check reads them. A change to either file during `fence` can leave `activation_fence_held` true and still pass verification. Activator mode compares the fence preserved state with `_preserved_ok`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n             and (fence.get(\"record_after_refusal\") or {}).get(\"sha256\")\n-            == fence_record.get(\"sha256\"))\n+            == fence_record.get(\"sha256\"))\n+        checks[\"fence_state_preserved\"] = _preserved_ok(\n+            fence.get(\"preserved\"), prepared, \"fence\", problems)\n```\n\n</details>","id":"92945df442ced33df3db45abc420bf8a73789ef4d9668ba9128fd26a337d86f0","intervals":[[3324,3325]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch.py","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Compare the fence-phase state digests with the prepared baseline."}],"head":"763808c0249c3a868fe16ae9159ca6c1f2e67ba6","head_tree":"e808aac5adf61e3f0f06365372f81340b3333575","input_scope":[{"blob":"6bab0c2a318551d8629b312c4d7207e80efe1cbb","intervals":[[1,3602]],"path":"apps/crq-python/ops/vm-unit-switch.py"}],"job_id":"69131df53fdabd49d50